# generated by make_cpl_config.py -- stage-3 coupled fine-tune
# atm parent E01-FT.aug26.atm.A0_B32_C0_L0_O5_W0_X0.S01   (same as E18-CFT)
# ocn parent E12-FT.aug26.ocn.A0_B16_C0_L0_O5_W1_X0.S01   (differs from E18-CFT)
#
# The ocean-loss-weighting arm at stage 3. Against E18-CFT the config differs
# in exactly one line -- the ocean's parameter_init.weights_path -- so whatever
# separates them comes from the ocean seed alone.
#
# Two caveats worth carrying into the analysis:
#
# 1. E12-FT is a B16 run and E18-CFT's ocean parent (E11-FT) is B32, so the
#    contrast is not W alone. At stage 2 the batch gap is the larger of the
#    two effects: E11-FT B32 scores 0.050938 on inference and E11-FT B16
#    scores 0.048804, while W1 (E12-FT, B16) scores 0.048685 against that same
#    B16 W0 baseline. The clean control is a coupled run seeded from E11-FT
#    B16 S01, which is finished and idle; it is not E18-CFT.
#
# 2. W1's per-variable weights (sst, ssh, ocean_sea_ice_fraction,
#    iceVolumeTotal at 2.0) do not carry into this stage. The coupled ocean
#    loss is EnsembleLoss(crps 0.9 / energy_score 0.1) with no weights, the
#    same as E18-CFT. So this asks whether a W1-trained ocean *seeds* a better
#    coupled model, not whether W1 weighting helps during coupling.
#
# Both realms initialize from best_inference_ckpt.tar. Verified healthy rather
# than assumed: E12-FT wrote that checkpoint 5 times, most recently 09-07
# 13:16, and E01-FT B32 wrote it 5 times through epoch 19 -- neither shows the
# rollout divergence that makes best_inference_ckpt meaningless for a stage-1
# checkpoint, and that the B32-L1 atm arm does show.
FME_NODES=8
FME_RANKS=32
FME_PRIORITY=1
WANDB_NAME=E20-CFT.aug26.cpl.A0_B32_C0_L0_O5_W1_X0.S01
WANDB_RUN_GROUP=aug26.cpl.E20-CFT
WANDB_JOB_TYPE=A0_B32_C0_L0_O5_W1_X0_CFT
WANDB_TAGS=cft,stage3,aug26,E20,cpl,A0,B32,C0,L0,O5,W1,X0,S01
WANDB_NOTES="stage-3 coupled fine-tune of E01-FT.aug26.atm.A0_B32_C0_L0_O5_W0_X0.S01 (atm) x E12-FT B16 W1 (ocn), both from best_inference_ckpt.tar | ocean loss-weighting arm vs E18-CFT | 8 nodes, 32 ranks, 50 epochs"
